# yq3 -- editing YAML without breaking it
#
# sed on YAML ends in tears. yq can rewrite a file in place and keep
# comments, key order and formatting:
#
#   yq -i --from-file update.yq values.yaml
#
# (The check runs that on a scratch copy, so your values.yaml stays as is.)
#
# Task, for the production release:
#   - set image.tag to "1.5.0"         (a string: the chart quotes it)
#   - set replicaCount to 3            (a number, not a string!)
#   - add the pod label  team: platform
#   - delete the whole `debug` block   (look up `del(...)`)
#
# Chain updates with `|`. The draft below gets the types wrong and forgets
# half the job. Try it: yq --from-file update.yq values.yaml
#

.image.tag = 1.5 |
.replicaCount = "3"
